               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding our shared patient, a 78-year-old female admitted on 2024-04-15 due to an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced exercise tolerance. Chest auscultation revealed diffuse expiratory wheezing bilaterally. Diagnostic workup included chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and spirometry, confirming obstructive ventilatory impairment with hypoxaemia. She was treated with inhaled short-acting bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy, leading to satisfactory clinical improvement. She was discharged on 2024-04-16 in stable condition with optimised inhaler therapy. I recommend close follow-up, review of maintenance bronchodilator regimen, and pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Please do not hesitate to contact me should you require further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
